menu "Knob moon display"

config KNOB_MOON_TEST_EPOCH
    int "UTC epoch for the static frame (until knob_time lands, K7d)"
    default 1794175200
    help
        The K7b static moon renders this UTC instant (default
        2026-11-08T22:00Z -- the milestone's bench date, so the disk
        can be compared against the published phase of the day).
        K7d's knob_time (esp_sntp over the existing Wi-Fi join)
        replaces this with the real instant; until then the moon view
        never claims a "now" it does not have.

config KNOB_MOON_SWEEP_FRAMES
    int "Cold-boot synodic sweep frame count (0 = static only)"
    default 1344
    range 0 4096
    help
        The new moon -> now sweep played on COLD boots only
        (deep-sleep wakes show the current phase, the clock's wake
        policy). 1344 = the clock's task #17 no-jump count: 336-frame
        sweeps showed a visible per-frame illumination jump, and the
        angular step is resolution-independent. The frame cost is
        roughly linear in this count -- measure it on the bench
        (K7c) before raising it on a battery product. 0 (or 1)
        disables the sweep entirely (bench builds).

config KNOB_MOON_SWEEP_BAKE_PX
    int "Intermediate sweep frame bake size (px)"
    default 128
    range 96 360
    help
        Intermediate sweep frames bake at this square edge (bake cost
        ~px^2) and upscale nearest-neighbour; the FINAL frame always
        bakes crisp at the panel's 360. Never below 96 -- the clock's
        measured sharpness floor (the terminator goes soft).

endmenu
